  "schema": "sunfold.cutout-clips/2",
  "note": "Poses are authored once in profile semantics, as if the figure faced screen-right, and every facing scales them through `viewGain`. Positive degrees are counter-clockwise on screen: a limb pointing down swings toward screen-right. Timing follows the AoE2 measurements already recorded in Docs/Architecture/aoe2-sprite-pipeline.md - walk 4 keys at 10 fps, gather and build 6 keys at 5 fps.",
  "gainNote": "`reachA`/`reachB` are separate and signed because the two arms need OPPOSITE rotations in a frontal view. In profile both arms reach forward with the same sign; face the camera and the same rotation that brings the screen-right arm down across the body throws the screen-left arm up and out. The sign flips again for the back view, where the tool arm reads on the other side of the screen. Walk legs no longer use FK `foot`/`swing` gains \u2014 they are driven by cyninja-style gait IK (`stride`/`lift` scaled by those keys so profile keeps a full stride while frontal facings scissor).",
